From f4c92586c03439010d17b7bf1671874f07d9a84a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: int3re <118649905+int3re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 02:27:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] curlpro: the device profile's plumbing; WebGL strings and
 limits

The driver passes --curlpro-fingerprint=<base64 JSON>, the browser
forwards it to renderers, blink::curlpro::Fingerprint reads it once.
WebGL serves the profile's UNMASKED_VENDOR/RENDERER, and its limits
only where they are lower than this GPU's own.
